From: Lee Duncan <lduncan@suse.com>
Date: Tue 01 Sep 2026 08:02:59 AM PDT
References: CVE-2026-74555 bsc#1275690
Patch-mainline: Never (kABI fixup)
Subject: scsi: libsas: fix sas_resume_ha_no_sync removal

Commit 66bdb0a40165 ("scsi: libsas: Fix HA resume deadlock and hisi_sas
disk-wake race (CVE-2026-74555 bsc#1275690).") removed
sas_resume_ha_no_sync() and all it's callers, but add it back in, for
kABI compatibility. Just call the updated common sas_resume_ha()
routine if this old function gets called, as the deadlock fixed
by that commit is no longer possible anyway.

Signed-off-by: Lee Duncan <lduncan@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/scsi/libsas/sas_init.c |   11 +++++++++++
 include/scsi/libsas.h          |    3 +++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/scsi/libsas/sas_init.c
+++ b/drivers/scsi/libsas/sas_init.c
@@ -462,6 +462,17 @@ void sas_resume_ha(struct sas_ha_struct
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(sas_resume_ha);
 
+/*
+ * Originally, a no-sync variant, which does not call sas_drain_ha().
+ *
+ * Removed upstream, but kept here for kabi compatibility.
+ */
+void sas_resume_ha_no_sync(struct sas_ha_struct *ha)
+{
+	sas_resume_ha(ha);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(sas_resume_ha_no_sync);
+
 void sas_suspend_ha(struct sas_ha_struct *ha)
 {
 	int i;
--- a/include/scsi/libsas.h
+++ b/include/scsi/libsas.h
@@ -684,6 +684,9 @@ extern void sas_prep_resume_ha(struct sa
 extern void sas_resume_ha(struct sas_ha_struct *sas_ha);
 extern void sas_suspend_ha(struct sas_ha_struct *sas_ha);
 
+/* for kABI compatibility: */
+extern void sas_resume_ha_no_sync(struct sas_ha_struct *sas_ha);
+
 int sas_set_phy_speed(struct sas_phy *phy, struct sas_phy_linkrates *rates);
 int sas_phy_reset(struct sas_phy *phy, int hard_reset);
 int sas_phy_enable(struct sas_phy *phy, int enable);
